[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=View or run with Tandem
Name[pt_BR]=Ver ou executar com Tandem
Name[es]=Ver o ejecutar con Tandem
Name[fr]=Voir ou lancer avec Tandem
Name[zh_CN]=用 Tandem 查看或运行
Name[hi]=Tandem से देखें या चलाएँ
Name[ar]=العرض أو التشغيل بواسطة Tandem
Comment=Show what this script does before anything runs it
Comment[pt_BR]=Mostra o que este script faz antes de qualquer coisa executá-lo
Comment[es]=Muestra lo que hace este script antes de que algo lo ejecute
Comment[fr]=Montre ce que fait ce script avant que quoi que ce soit ne l'exécute
Comment[zh_CN]=在任何东西运行它之前，先显示这个脚本做什么
Comment[hi]=कोई इसे चलाने से पहले दिखाता है कि यह स्क्रिप्ट क्या करती है
Comment[ar]=يُظهر ما يفعله هذا النصّ البرمجي قبل أن يشغّله أي شيء
Exec=/usr/bin/tandem-script %f
Icon=tandem
Terminal=false
NoDisplay=false
Categories=System;
# There is deliberately NO MimeType line here, and removing one would be a
# regression rather than a tidy-up.
#
# Declaring application/x-shellscript is not neutral: with no explicit default in
# mimeapps.list the desktop database picks a handler FROM these lines, so merely
# naming the type takes it. Measured on this machine - the type belonged to a text
# editor, and after installing a build that named it here it belonged to Tandem.
#
# Opening a downloaded script in a text editor is a defensible default, and this
# project does not take a type away from a handler already doing the right thing.
# tandem-script stays reachable through "tandem install file.sh", through the
# panel's file chooser, and through "Open with -> Other Application", which lists
# every installed program regardless of what it declares.
